From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:26:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: Cancel a vblank FIFO sample that waits too
 long

EXPERIMENT fix, on top of patch 0012.

The FIFO sampler is a drm_vblank_work. When vblanks stop coming (display
interrupts lost, see patch 0015), it stays queued, and
drm_vblank_work_flush_all() in intel_atomic_commit_tail() waits for the
queue to drain without a timeout: the next commit (sway turning the
output off to recover) hung in D state for good, before the crtc disable
that would have cycled the power well. The poller already noticed a
sample pending for over 200 ms but only cleared its flag; cancel the
work too, which also wakes a commit waiting in flush_all.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
index 91fc724..b64d6bd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
@@ -1060,7 +1060,15 @@ static void vlv_dsi_underrun_work(struct work_struct *work)
 			ur->fifo_pending = false;
 	} else if (ur->fifo_pending &&
 		   ktime_sub(now, ur->fifo_last_sched) > 200 * NSEC_PER_MSEC) {
-		/* cancelled by a vblank off we did not see */
+		/*
+		 * Cancelled by a vblank off we did not see, or still queued
+		 * for a vblank that does not come (lost display interrupts).
+		 * A queued work blocks drm_vblank_work_flush_all(), which every
+		 * commit waits in without a timeout, so take it off the queue.
+		 */
+		if (drm_vblank_work_cancel_sync(&ur->fifo_work))
+			drm_info(display->drm,
+				 "DSI DPI FIFO vblank sample: no vblank for 200 ms, sample cancelled\n");
 		ur->fifo_pending = false;
 	}
 
